From 3b5ec102e6d59c20c3686f6147ccaf88ae30572f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:26:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] blt-action owns /assign; blt-pool drops its copy and its
 GitHub sweep

Issue #38: BLT-Action and BLT-Pool both had /assign. BLT-Action (forge workflow
blt-action--assign.yml) is now the only one.

blt-pool (blt-github-app Worker):
- /assign and /unassign are ignored (no reaction, no reply). /approve still
  assigns the last person who commented /assign.
- Removed _assign, _unassign, the 2-hourly _run_scheduled sweep
  (_check_stale_assignments, _check_stale_mentor_assignments) and the helpers
  only it used. It walked every GitHub App installation and polled the frozen
  OWASP-BLT/* GitHub repositories. on_scheduled now runs only the
  forge-leaderboard task; any other call logs and returns.

blt-cron: dropped the "blt-pool" 0 */2 job. The blt-pool-leaderboard task stays.

blt-action: ported the stale-assignment release that BLT-Pool and the old
GitHub Action had (docs said "Nothing unassigns stale issues automatically").
forge/stale.mjs runs daily (.forkmesh/blt-action--unassign-stale.yml, 05:53
UTC, job API only, no commit). For self-claims only (/assign or the web claim
button; never a maintainer's assignment), with no pull request in the forge
pulls ledger and no comment from the assignee for 6 days, it posts one warning.
At 7 days, once the warning is at least 20 hours old, it unassigns and says
so. A comment from the assignee restarts the clock. If the pulls ledger can't
be read, the run changes nothing. The /assign reply now mentions this.

Tests: forge/stale.test.mjs (10), the pool comment-routing and on_scheduled
tests, and the blt-cron job list.

Fixes #38

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
